1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means all source code, binaries, build scripts,
   configuration files, disk images, installer media, virtual machine
   images, container images, update packages, and any other
   machine-readable materials that WSDS makes available in this repository
   or through any other channel, including release downloads, the
   Software's own updater, archives, and mirrors. It includes every copy,
   including a copy installed or running on a machine.

   "Documentation" means all design documents, architecture
   specifications, research materials, diagrams, technical writing, and
   any other human-readable materials that WSDS makes available with the
   Software, including but not limited to files in the docs/ directory and
   any markdown files (.md).

   "Materials" means the Software and Documentation collectively, in any
   form and wherever you obtained them.

   "Non-Commercial Use" means either of the following, when it is not part
   of the operations of a business and is not offered to others as a
   product or service: (a) personal use by an individual, including
   personal evaluation, non-commercial experimentation, and hobby use; or
   (b) use by an Academic Institution, or by its students, faculty, or
   staff in that role, for teaching, study, or non-commercial research. A
   Non-Commercial Use may be continuous. Keeping an installation running
   around the clock for one of these purposes does not make it a
   commercial or production use, and an Academic Institution's use does
   not become commercial because the institution charges tuition or
   receives grant funding.

   "Academic Institution" means a college, university, or other
   degree-granting institution of higher education, or a non-profit
   research institution.

   "Third-Party Component" means software, firmware, microcode, fonts,
   data, model files, or any other item that someone other than WSDS owns
   and that is included in, built into, or distributed with the Software.
   Examples are the Linux kernel, GRUB, BusyBox, Git, OpenSSH, OpenSSL,
   curl, wpa_supplicant, eudev, Mesa, WPE WebKit, cog, llama.cpp, the
   linux-firmware collection, Intel and AMD processor microcode, the Rust
   toolchain, the sentence-embedding model inside an image, xterm.js, and
   the open source Rust crates the Software is built from.

   "Third-Party Model" means an AI model that someone other than WSDS
   owns, with its weights, parameters, tokenizer, and related files, that
   the Software can download, import, load, or connect to at your
   direction. It includes the model as its licensor published it and as
   WSDS or anyone else has converted, quantized, or otherwise modified it.
   A model file that ships inside an image of the Software is a
   Third-Party Component.

   "Native Model" means a Third-Party Model that the Software runs on your
   Hardware itself.

   "Model Terms" means, for a Third-Party Model, the license, the
   acceptable use policy, and any other terms that its licensor applies to
   it, as the licensor changes them from time to time.

   "Third-Party Service" means a service that WSDS does not operate and
   that the Software can connect to, such as a model provider or model
   server, a search, media, or code-hosting service, a model repository, a
   download or update host, or a time server.

   "Intelligence" means an AI system instance that the Software runs, with
   its sealed identity, memory, sessions, and tools.

   "Output" means anything that an Intelligence or a model generates or
   does, including text, code, images, decisions, tool calls, scheduled
   jobs, and actions taken on your Hardware, in your accounts, or on other
   systems.

   "Operator Content" means content that you create or supply for use with
   the Software, such as identity and knowledge files, memories, sessions,
   workspace files, settings, credentials, certificates, and dynamic tools
   that you write or approve. It does not include any part of the
   Materials.

   "Hardware" means any physical or virtual machine on which you install
   or run the Software, and any device, storage, network, or other
   equipment attached to it or reachable from it.

   "System" means the Materials together with every Third-Party Component,
   Third-Party Model, and Third-Party Service used with them, every
   Intelligence the Software runs, and all Output.

   "WSDS Parties" means WSDS and its owners, members, managers, officers,
   employees, contractors, agents, successors, and assigns.

   "You" means the individual who accesses or uses the Materials and any
   organization on whose behalf that individual does so.

