SCHEDULE A: THIRD-PARTY MODEL TERMS FOR NATIVE MODELS

As of November 26, 2026

A.1 ABOUT NATIVE MODELS

   Native Models are an experimental feature. The files that WSDS makes
   available for a Native Model are modified from the licensor's own:
   converted to the file format the Software's model server reads and, in
   most cases, quantized. Unless a licensor says otherwise, it has not
   tested or approved them.

   A Native Model, and a small or quantized one in particular, answers
   more slowly and with less judgment than a large hosted model. It is
   more likely to state false information, to misuse or invent tool calls,
   and to follow instructions hidden in content it reads. WSDS has not
   vetted the Native Models against the Software's full set of tools, and
   the Guardian's replicant check does not run while a Native Model leads
   an Intelligence. Supervise an Intelligence that a Native Model leads,
   and do not give it access that you cannot afford to have misused.

